<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Balkans and Hungary</p><h1 class="st-title">Albanian Kingdom</h1><p class="st-meta">1928 CE – 1939 CE · capital Tirana</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Albania's only native monarchy, the kingdom of Zog I, which modernised the country's laws while falling ever deeper under Italian control.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>On 1 September 1928 a constituent assembly turned the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/albanian-republic">Albanian Republic</a> into a kingdom, and President <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zog-i">Ahmet Zogu</a> became Zog I, King of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/albanians">Albanians</a>, a title chosen to suggest claims beyond the state's borders. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tirana">Tirana</a> remained the capital, and the strong presidential powers of 1925 passed to the crown.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zog-i">Zog</a> ruled as an authoritarian moderniser, introducing civil and penal codes based on Italian, French and Swiss models, separating religion from the state and banning the face veil in 1937. Schools, roads and a small army were built, largely with Italian loans and advisers, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> controlled the oil concessions and the national bank. Revolts, such as that at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fier">Fier</a> in 1935, were suppressed.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benito-mussolini">Mussolini</a> invaded on 7 April 1939, and resistance collapsed within days. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zog-i">Zog</a> fled with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/geraldine-of-albania">Queen Geraldine</a> and their newborn son, never to return. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> turned the country into the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/albanian-kingdom-1939-1943">Albanian Kingdom</a> (1939-1943) under King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/victor-emmanuel-iii">Victor Emmanuel III</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/albanian-kingdom.jpg" alt="Albanian Kingdom" width="320" height="214"><figcaption>Image: Orange Tuesday (Later version was uploaded by AceDouble) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Albania_(1928%E2%80%931934).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1928 CE – 1939 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Tirana</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Zog I</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam, Orthodox and Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Albanian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/albania">Albania</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kingdom of Albania (1928-1939), Zogist Albania</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1934&amp;focus=albanian-kingdom" aria-label="Albanian Kingdom on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5164 704 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Albanian Kingdom lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5484 960L5484 960M5484 960L5304 942"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5484 960h0M5304 942h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5484 960h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5484 960h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Tirana. <a href="/atlas?year=1934&amp;focus=albanian-kingdom">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
